Here is the commit message:
SOLR-4218: SolrTestCaseJ4 throws NPE when closing the core
 (on the afterClass method)

git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/lucene/dev/trunk@1423932 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the `SolrTestCaseJ4` attempting to close the core in the `afterClass` method, which led to a null pointer exception when the `defaultClient` or `loadbalancer` was not initialized (i.e., null) at that point, and their respective `shutdown()` methods were called without null checks.

Here is the patch:

   @Override
   public void close() {
     try {
       ExecutorUtil.shutdownAndAwaitTermination(commExecutor);
     } catch (Throwable e) {
       SolrException.log(log, e);
     }

     try {
-      defaultClient.getConnectionManager().shutdown();
+      if(defaultClient != null) {
+        defaultClient.getConnectionManager().shutdown();
+      }
     } catch (Throwable e) {
       SolrException.log(log, e);
     }
     try {
-      loadbalancer.shutdown();
+      if(loadbalancer != null) {
+        loadbalancer.shutdown();
+      }
     } catch (Throwable e) {
       SolrException.log(log, e);
     }

   }
 }


