The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
defaultClient.getConnectionManager().shutdown();
loadbalancer.shutdown();
```
Reason:
The `SolrTestCaseJ4` class attempts to call the `shutdown()` methods on `defaultClient` and `loadbalancer` without checking if they are null, leading to a NullPointerException (NPE) if either of these objects is not initialized.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
if(defaultClient != null) {
    defaultClient.getConnectionManager().shutdown();
}
if(loadbalancer != null) {
    loadbalancer.shutdown();
}
```
Reason:
The added null checks before calling the `shutdown()` methods ensure that the methods are only invoked if `defaultClient` and `loadbalancer` are not null, thus preventing the NullPointerException and allowing the `close()` method to execute safely.

